The TypeScript adaptation accepts only constant decimal option values (no
expressions or suffixes), refuses timeline enable and runtime commands, always
writes a new owned frame instead of filtering in place, and makes the x86-64
conversion of a non-finite or out-of-range double (INT64_MIN, clipped to
INT32_MIN) explicit. It adds no FFmpeg runtime code.
The original source and full notices remain in the pinned upstream submodule.
